// Rule: [T1048] Safepay - B2 Exfiltration Tool
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1048
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Hunting query for b2 exfiltration tool, with evidence boundaries and target-environment validation requirements
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for b2 exfiltration tool using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A match proves only process execution; it does not prove exfiltration, ransomware activity, or attribution.
// A match does not prove: A match proves only process execution; it does not prove exfiltration, ransomware activity, or attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Classification: Hunting | Confidence: Medium | Logic: Campaign-specific artifact
// Joint advisory AA26-293A states SafePay actors executed commands via b2.exe to exfiltrate victim data.
// A match proves only process execution; it does not prove exfiltration, ransomware activity, or attribution.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "b2.exe"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountDomain, AccountName,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine, SHA1,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessAccountName, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
